  <conditions attached="1">
   <condition type="2">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funds must be used for the agreed immunisation activities (hepatitis B vaccines; health-system strengthening and cold-chain support; COVID-19 vaccine support), meeting the programmatic, coverage and equity targets and the monitoring and reporting requirements set out in the Gavi funding guidelines, co-financing policy and any decision letters issued for the country, the joint appraisal and annual progress reporting.</narrative>
   </condition>
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gavi support to Ukraine is conditional on alignment with the national immunisation strategy and comprehensive multi-year plan, and on compliance with Gavi&apos;s eligibility, transition and sustainability policies. The applicable policy conditions are set out in the Gavi funding guidelines, co-financing policy and any decision letters issued for the country.</narrative>
   </condition>
   <condition type="3">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine must meet its vaccine co-financing obligations and comply with financial management, funds-flow, audit and data-quality requirements. The specific co-financing amounts and fiduciary terms are set out in the Gavi co-financing policy and the Gavi funding guidelines, co-financing policy and any decision letters issued for the country.</narrative>
   </condition>
  </conditions>
